# Clinical write authority and prescription integrity (rule 228)

**Status:** scope of `DMS-RME-REVISION-PROGRAM-8C` (2026-11-07). Sprint record:
`docs/sprints/dms-rme-revision-program-8c.md`. Owner decisions of the Program 8 owner-decision checkpoint
(`DMS-RME-REVISION-PROGRAM-8-OWNER-OPERATIONAL-CLOSURE-1`, 2026-11-07): D3 Group 1 "FIX NOW", D3-NEW-4 "FIX NOW".
Category under the Foundation-First Sprint Lock: security fix / clinical correctness.

This rule EXTENDS rules 138, 226 and 227. Where they differ, this rule wins:

- rule 226 §1 and rule 227 §3 said prescriptions carry "no room rule" (OD-7-2 open) — §1 below adds it;
- rule 227 §1.3 said every account that is not a context-bound non-clinical one keeps the RME-wide document read —
  §5 below narrows that to an allowlist;
- rule 138's room scope bound the visit, the RME page and the odontogram — §1 and §2 extend it to prescriptions and
  to the live-encounter write authority. Its §17 boundary (history is never room-hidden) is unchanged.

## 1. Prescriptions follow the doctor room scope (OD-7-2, R8A-1)

1. `RmePrescriptionPolicy` (`view`, `print`, `viewForVisit`, `create`, `update`) applies the doctor-patient scope and
   then `DoctorRoomScopeService::authorizeActiveVisitRoom()`: a doctor never opens or writes the prescription of an
   ACTIVE visit (registered / waiting / in_progress) of another treatment room.
2. `PrescriptionAuthoringAuthority::permits()` re-asserts it (`deniesActiveVisitOutsideRoom()`), so a caller that skips
   the route and the policy is refused the same way (CG-06).
3. Post-examination and historical visits (cashier_pending, completed, cancelled) are never room-restricted, and an
   account that is not doctor-scoped (Supervisor RME, Owner, Super Admin) is unaffected.

## 2. The live-encounter write authority is room scoped (OD-5-7)

1. `RmeVisitConsentService::actorMayWorkOnEncounter()` — the single predicate behind current-RME writes, handwriting,
   odontogram charting and performed treatments — refuses a doctor whose live room is not the encounter's room. The
   current-RME write is keyed on the patient's canonical record book, so it never reached the visit's room guard.
2. A doctor with no live room context is refused on an ACTIVE encounter (fail closed), as rule 138 already refuses the
   visit page itself.

## 3. Starting an examination is a clinical act (OD-5-2)

1. `ClinicVisitPolicy::startExamination()` is the clinical examination authority (`complete_rme_examination` + working
   branch + doctor-patient scope — the same as `completeExamination()`). The controller authorizes it for
   `in_progress`, and `ClinicVisitService::transitionStatus()` re-asserts it for every caller.
2. The front desk keeps CANCEL (a no-show): `cancelled` is not gated by it.
3. The visit page offers "Mulai Pemeriksaan" only to an account that holds the ability; hiding it is not the boundary.

## 4. A finished examination keeps its doctor (OD-5-3)

`ClinicVisitService::assignRoom()` on a `cashier_pending` visit moves only the room; `doctor_id` and the
patient-doctor assignment stay with the doctor who examined. Pre-examination placement still resolves the online
doctor of the room exactly as before. Terminal visits stay refused.

## 5. Role allowlists, not denylists (D3-NEW-1, D3-NEW-4)

1. RME / odontogram / performed-treatment authoring requires a role in `FrontOfficeRole::CLINICAL_ROLES` (the same list
   prescriptions use, rule 227 §3) on top of `manage_clinic_visits`. A role created at runtime and given
   `manage_clinic_visits` (production holds one, `Tester RME`, no holders) does not inherit authoring.
2. Cross-branch clinical-document READ is `RmeWorkingBranchScope::CROSS_BRANCH_DOCUMENT_READ_ROLES` (clinical roles +
   Owner). The context-bound front desk and cashier keep their working branch (rule 227 §1.2); any other account reads
   NO clinical document until it is classified. A new role that must read across branches is added on purpose.
3. Every seeded role that holds a clinic-visit permission is classified — pinned by
   `RmeClinicalDocumentReadScopeAllowlistTest` A-05.

## 6. Not changed by §1–§5

No schema, migration, permission, role, route or package change. No flag, enforcement scope, branch lock, queue
worker, scheduler or KTP timer change. The Program 8B foundations (rule 227 §1–§4) are unchanged except where this
rule narrows them.

## 7. Critical-gate coverage (CI-8C)

`RmeClinicalWriteAuthorityTest` is selected by the new `RmeClinicalWriteAuthority` token in BOTH critical-gate filter
variants; `RmeClinicalDocumentReadScopeAllowlistTest` is selected by the existing `RmeClinicalDocumentReadScope`
token. Both are declared in `config/ci_runner.php` `critical_gate_mandatory_suites`.
